      "problem": "${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\sqrt[3]{x}=$",
      "worked_solution": "Let $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x}.$ Let's sketch the graph of $y=f(x):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14267961/assets/35cd7d1487285bcb2094325ab052a2a2eb13dfe8191ec125118387bc9d7a93d5.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the function increases without bound as $x$ increases. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x)=\\infty .\n$$",
