      "problem": "${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\sqrt{x+3}=$",
      "worked_solution": "Let $f(x)=\\sqrt{x+3}.$ Let's sketch the graph of $y=f(x):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14267961/assets/b03d3bc42d076a63937ab41d939c6d39ceca8bdb879c9ed58d583ab8a694a979.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the function increases without bound as $x$ increases. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x)=\\infty .\n$$",
